## What the user provides

The e-mail address and password of their {{ vendor_name }} app account (`descriptor.py`). Change the credential fields to what the vendor really needs (an application key and secret, a brand choice, ...); every text is English and German.

## Capabilities

| Feature | Supported |
| --- | --- |
| State (activity, battery, charging, error code with category) | yes |
| Start (start plan `now`), pause, resume, return to the dock | yes |
| Emergency stop | yes, as an immediate pause (sent even when the vendor reports the mower offline) |
| Map areas, patterns, manual driving, blade height, speed, light, camera, settings, firmware, maintenance | no (not declared, so MowDeck refuses and hides them) |

Declare more in `connection.py` only together with its implementation; the conformance kit checks both directions.

## Layout

| Module | Role |
| --- | --- |
| `plugin.py` | `SPEC`, the `mowdeck.cloud_providers` entry point (imports no SDK) |
| `provider.py` | the `CloudProviderPlugin`: descriptor, discovery, connections |
| `descriptor.py` | credential fields, guidance, texts in English and German |
| `connection.py` | the `MowerConnection`: capabilities, state mapping, commands |
| `client.py` | the port to the vendor cloud (no SDK types) |
| `sdk_client.py` | the real client on `{{ sdk_module }}` (a stub until wired in) |
| `fake_client.py` | the fake cloud: accounts `*@fake.mowdeck.test`, password `fake-cloud-password`, one online and one offline mower |
| `lexicon.py` | the error lexicon (`mowdeck.error_lexicons`), empty until filled from the SDK's table |

## Tests

`uv run pytest libs/{{ distribution }}`: `tests/test_{{ vendor }}_conformance.py` runs the provider conformance kit (`mowdeck-provider-testkit`) on the fake cloud, `tests/test_{{ vendor }}_connection.py` the rules the kit cannot know. No network, no vendor account.
